   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to providing\nfor a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S9693",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9693-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9693\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nproviding for a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on\ncertain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law allowing the State Liquor\nAuthority to issue a license to a hotel located at 428 S 5th STREET,\nBROOKLYN NY 11211 with the entrance located on SOUTH 5th STREET, just\nsouthwest of HEWES STREET.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends subdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alcoholic Beverage\nControl Law by adding a new paragraph which allows a license for on\npremises consumption of alcoholic beverages at restaurants located with-\nin the building which serves as a hotel but is within 200 feet of a\nschool\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis hotel has been operating since 2022 and currently is permitted to\nserve beer and wine. They wish to obtain a liquor license. Since the\nentrance is within 200 feet of BNYOS CHAYIL school, legislation allowing\nan exemption is required. This application has the support of the Bnyos\nChayil school as well as other community members and organizations.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE: :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
